  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is positive (0.00–0.67) and model shows over-optimism (e.g., overshoots recent highs).",
    "Reduce forecast volatility in early periods (e.g., 1–3 days) when sentiment is neutral or slightly negative; avoid sharp spikes.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias for 3–5 day horizons if model consistently overpredicts after a spike (e.g., 70+ → 68–70).",
    "Increase downward bias for 10+ day horizons when sentiment is neutral or negative, especially if recent prices are trending upward.",
    "Correct for lagged response: if true outcome is higher than forecasted 3–5 days later, reduce forecast by 0.5–1.5% for next 3–7 day horizon.",
    "Avoid overreacting to sentiment spikes: if sentiment jumps to 0.67+ but price doesn’t follow, reduce forecast by 1–2% to prevent overshoot."
  ]
}
